<article class="env-lemma" id="0BVZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BVZ">Lemma <span data-tag="0BVZ">49.7.4</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Let $n \geq 1$ and $f_1, \ldots , f_ n \in A[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]$. Set $B = A[x_1, \ldots , x_ n]/(f_1, \ldots , f_ n)$. The Kähler different of $B$ over $A$ is the ideal of $B$ generated by $\det (\partial f_ i/\partial x_ j)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $\Omega _{B/A}$ has a presentation 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \bigoplus \nolimits _{i = 1, \ldots , n} B f_ i \xrightarrow {\text{d}} \bigoplus \nolimits _{j = 1, \ldots , n} B \text{d}x_ j \rightarrow \Omega _{B/A} \rightarrow 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00RU" data-tag="00RU">10.131.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>